{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-knot-factor-borromean-composite","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:knot-factor-borromean-composite","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of knot factor borromean composite","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-knot-factor-borromean-composite"],"text":"knot-factor-borromean-composite-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:knot-factor-borromean-composite\"></a><p>Brunnian-ness decouples the Hecke pairings of distinct\ncomponents: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_\\lambda(\\beta_{\\mathrm{Bor}_k}) =\n\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\chi_\\lambda(\\beta_{4_1}^{(i)})</code> on each Wedderburn\nblock.  Substituting in\n(<a href=\"#prop:knot-factor-spectral-form\" data-at=\"mass-theory/plancherel-knot-factor-mass-tower\">knot factor</a>) and applying the\namphicheiral corollary\n(<a href=\"#cor:knot-factor-amphicheiral\" data-at=\"mass-theory/plancherel-knot-factor-mass-tower\">amphicheiral</a>) componentwise gives\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1 - h^2)^k</code>.  <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n<p><strong>Application.</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^4\\mathrm{He}</code> is a Borromean-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> configuration;\nits knot factor is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1 - h^2)^2</code>, a derived value.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-borromean-composite-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-knot-factor-borromean-composite","qa":{"counts":{"pass":56,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":58},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
